    "terrainName": "village-street",
    "description": "The street fight of a real-data town, on an anonymized 800 x 500 m extract of that town ('village-street': its streets, house spacing, buildings, doors, windows and trees as in the source; the map frame is arbitrary and the heights are shifted). An 18 m wide straight street (y 255, between x 300 and 680): 'Red Platoon' (Hostile) runs PlatoonDefend around (550, 255) with a T-72, a ZU-23 technical and the radar SAM; 'Blue Platoon' (Friend, under 'Blue HQ' with SupportCommand) runs PlatoonAttack from (390, 255) with an M1 and a Bradley following and an Apache in support. Behaviours as in the source run, nothing scripted. Observed there: the squads fight bunched in the open street, the base of fire leaves the house line for the street centre, suppression goes on with no ammunition and at dead targets, and dead men keep running behaviours."
  },
